1	# Patterns
2	
3	The parts every page repeats, written to pass the gates. Take the code's shape; the names, copy, values and composition are yours. `tokens.css`, `base.css` and the slot script come from the scaffold.
4	
5	## Controls, all eight states
6	
7	```css
8	.btn { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-xs); min-height: 48px; padding: 0 var(--space-lg); border: 1px solid var(--color-ink); border-radius: var(--radius-input, var(--radius-pill)); background: var(--color-ink); color: var(--color-paper); font: 500 var(--text-md)/1 var(--font-body); white-space: nowrap; text-decoration: none; cursor: pointer; transition: background-color var(--dur-short) var(--ease-out), transform var(--dur-micro) var(--ease-out); }
9	.btn:hover { background: var(--color-ink-2); }
10	.btn:active { transform: translateY(1px); }
11	.btn:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--color-focus); outline-offset: 2px; }
12	.btn:disabled, .btn[aria-disabled="true"] { opacity: 0.55; cursor: not-allowed; transform: none; }
13	.btn[aria-busy="true"] { cursor: progress; }
14	.btn--quiet { background: transparent; color: var(--color-ink); border-color: var(--color-rule); }
15	.btn--quiet:hover { background: var(--color-paper-2); }
16	@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .btn { transition: background-color var(--dur-short) linear; } }
17	```
18	
19	One filled primary a page (F4); the quiet one goes somewhere else. Error and success belong to the form, below.
20	
21	## A photograph in a slot
22	
23	```html
24	<figure class="photo" data-slot="hero" data-alt="The orchard in October, rows of trees heavy with fruit">
25	  <img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/.../1280px-....jpg"
26	       srcset=".../960px-....jpg 960w, .../1280px-....jpg 1280w, .../1920px-....jpg 1920w" sizes="(min-width: 60rem) 45vw, 100vw"
27	       width="4000" height="5000" alt="Rows of apple trees in October light" style="object-position: 50% 40%" fetchpriority="high">
28	</figure>
29	<p class="caption">Picking runs from September to the first frost.</p>
30	```
31	
32	```css
33	.photo { aspect-ratio: 4 / 5; min-height: 440px; margin: 0; border-radius: var(--radius-card); }
34	.photo > img { outline: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-ink) 8%, transparent); outline-offset: -1px; }
35	.caption { margin-top: var(--space-sm); font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--color-ink-2); }
36	```
37	
38	The `<img>` comes from `theme.mjs photos`; `base.css` supplies the cover fit, the loading wash and the theme's treatment. The credit goes in the footer's *Photographs* line; the caption is a fact from the prompt, outside the frame. A product sample takes the same kind of slot with no `<img>`: the interface built at full size (`imagery.md` § 4).
39	
40	## A choice between a few
41	
42	```html
43	<fieldset class="seg"><legend>Size</legend>
44	  <input type="radio" name="size" id="s1" value="1" checked><label for="s1">One box</label>
45	  <input type="radio" name="size" id="s2" value="2"><label for="s2">Two boxes</label>
46	</fieldset>
47	```
48	
49	```css
50	.seg input { position: absolute; opacity: 0; width: 1px; height: 1px; }
51	.seg label { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 44px; padding: 0 var(--space-md); border: 1px solid var(--color-rule); cursor: pointer; }
52	.seg input:checked + label { background: var(--color-ink); color: var(--color-paper); }
53	.seg input:focus-visible + label { outline: 2px solid var(--color-focus); outline-offset: 2px; }
54	```
55	
56	The radios stay in the flow at one pixel (53); the label carries the state and the ring, in the body face, sentence case.
57	
58	## A rail and a switcher
59	
60	```html
61	<ul class="rail" tabindex="0" aria-label="Upcoming dates">
62	  <li><time datetime="2027-06-12">12 June</time> Whitby</li>
63	  <!-- five or more items; the next one cut by the edge -->
64	</ul>
65	<div class="switch" data-switch>
66	  <div class="seg" role="tablist" aria-label="Menu"><button role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="m1" id="t1">Lunch</button><button role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="m2" id="t2" tabindex="-1">Dinner</button></div>
67	  <section role="tabpanel" id="m1" aria-labelledby="t1">...</section>
68	  <section role="tabpanel" id="m2" aria-labelledby="t2" hidden>...</section>
69	</div>
70	```
71	
72	```css
73	.rail { display: grid; grid-auto-flow: column; grid-auto-columns: minmax(16rem, 22%); gap: var(--gap-columns); overflow-x: auto; scroll-snap-type: x mandatory; scroll-padding-inline: var(--gutter); padding-inline: var(--gutter); overscroll-behavior-x: contain; }
74	.rail > * { scroll-snap-align: start; }
75	.rail:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--color-focus); outline-offset: 4px; }
76	```
77	
78	The rail scrolls by touch, wheel and arrow keys once focused, and sits outside the container's padding so its edge cuts the next item. The switcher's tabs move with the arrow keys (a few lines of script set `aria-selected`, `tabindex` and `hidden`); without script every panel shows in order. A pinned pair is `position: sticky; top: var(--space-2xl)` on the visual's column, released under 60rem.
79	
80	## A fact the prompt did not give
81	
82	```html
83	<p>Doors at <span class="fill" data-fill="time">time to be announced</span>, at <a href="#venue">the venue</a>.</p>
84	```
85	
86	```css
87	.fill { padding: 0 0.25em; border: 1px dashed color-mix(in oklch, var(--color-muted) 70%, transparent); border-radius: 3px; color: var(--color-muted); -webkit-box-decoration-break: clone; box-decoration-break: clone; }
88	```
89	
90	Two a page at most, each named in the handoff (`craft.md` § 8).
91	
92	## A form that posts nowhere yet
93	
94	```html
95	<form class="signup" data-endpoint="" novalidate>
96	  <label for="email">Email address</label>
97	  <div class="signup__row">
98	    <input id="email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required>
99	    <button class="btn" type="submit">Send me the date</button>
100	  </div>
101	  <p class="signup__help" id="email-help" aria-live="polite"></p>
102	</form>
103	```
104	
105	```js
106	document.querySelectorAll('form[data-endpoint]').forEach((form) => {
107	  const input = form.querySelector('input'), help = form.querySelector('[aria-live]');
108	  form.addEventListener('submit', (e) => {
109	    e.preventDefault();
110	    const ok = input.checkValidity();
111	    input.toggleAttribute('aria-invalid', !ok);
112	    if (!ok) { input.setAttribute('aria-describedby', help.id); help.textContent = 'That address looks incomplete. Write it as name@example.com.'; input.focus(); return; }
113	    if (!form.dataset.endpoint) { help.textContent = 'Nothing was sent: this form is not connected yet.'; return; }
114	    fetch(form.dataset.endpoint, { method: 'POST', body: new FormData(form) })
115	      .then((r) => { help.textContent = r.ok ? 'Thanks. The date goes to ' + input.value.trim() + '.' : 'That did not go through. Try again in a minute.'; })
116	      .catch(() => { help.textContent = 'That did not go through. Try again in a minute.'; });
117	  });
118	});
119	```
120	
121	```css
122	.signup__row { display: flex; gap: var(--space-xs); }
123	.signup input { flex: 1; min-width: 0; min-height: 48px; padding: 0 var(--space-md); border: 1px solid var(--color-muted); border-radius: var(--radius-input, var(--radius-pill)); background: var(--color-paper); color: var(--color-ink); outline: 2px solid transparent; outline-offset: -3px; }
124	.signup input:focus-visible { outline-color: var(--color-focus); }
125	.signup input[aria-invalid] { border-color: var(--color-error); }
126	.signup__help { min-height: 1lh; margin-top: var(--space-2xs); font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--color-muted); }
127	```
128	
129	## One reveal that survives no script
130	
131	```html
132	<script>document.documentElement.classList.add('js');</script>
133	```
134	
135	```css
136	.js [data-reveal] { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(8px); transition: opacity var(--dur-long) var(--ease-out), transform var(--dur-long) var(--ease-out); transition-delay: calc(var(--i, 0) * 40ms); }
137	.js [data-reveal].is-in { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
138	@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .js [data-reveal] { opacity: 1; transform: none; transition: none; } }
139	```
140	
141	```js
142	const io = new IntersectionObserver((es) => es.forEach((e) => { if (e.isIntersecting) { e.target.classList.add('is-in'); io.unobserve(e.target); } }), { rootMargin: '0px 0px -10% 0px' });
143	document.querySelectorAll('[data-reveal]').forEach((el) => io.observe(el));
144	```
145	
146	Visible with scripting off (62), at its end state under reduced motion, once, and only where the theme lets something move.
147	
148	## Figures that compare
149	
150	```css
151	.stats { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
152	.stats > * { padding-inline: var(--space-lg); border-left: 1px solid var(--color-rule); }
153	.stats > :first-child { padding-left: 0; border-left: 0; }
154	.stats b { display: block; font: 600 var(--text-3xl)/1 var(--font-display); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
155	@media (max-width: 60rem) { .stats { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); } .stats > * { padding: var(--space-md) 0; border-left: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule); } .stats > :first-child { border-top: 0; } }
156	```
157	
158	Only figures the user gave (46a), each with its unit and what it counts.
159	
160	## A loop that can pause
161	
162	Anything moving past 5 seconds (a marquee, an ambient loop, a looping video) holds still until the script runs, stops off-screen and under reduced motion, pauses on hover and focus, and carries a visible pause control (18, WCAG 2.2.2).
163	
164	```html
165	<figure data-loop>
166	  <!-- the drawing, the loop or the video -->
167	  <button class="btn btn--quiet" type="button" data-loop-toggle>Pause</button>
168	</figure>
169	```
170	
171	```css
172	[data-loop]:not(.is-running), [data-loop]:not(.is-running) *, [data-loop]:not(.is-running) *::before, [data-loop]:not(.is-running) *::after { animation-play-state: paused !important; }
173	html:not(.js) [data-loop-toggle] { display: none; }
174	@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { [data-loop-toggle] { display: none; } }
175	```
176	
177	```js
178	document.querySelectorAll('[data-loop]').forEach((el) => {
179	  const btn = el.querySelector('[data-loop-toggle]');
180	  const s = { seen: false, hover: false, focus: false, held: matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches };
181	  const sync = () => {
182	    const run = s.seen && !s.hover && !s.focus && !s.held;
183	    el.classList.toggle('is-running', run);
184	    el.querySelectorAll('video').forEach((v) => (run ? v.play().catch(() => {}) : v.pause()));
185	    btn.textContent = s.held ? 'Play' : 'Pause';
186	  };
187	  btn.addEventListener('click', () => { s.held = !s.held; sync(); });
188	  [['pointerenter', 'hover', true], ['pointerleave', 'hover', false], ['focusin', 'focus', true], ['focusout', 'focus', false]].forEach(([t, k, v]) => el.addEventListener(t, () => { s[k] = v; sync(); }));
189	  new IntersectionObserver(([e]) => { s.seen = e.isIntersecting; sync(); }).observe(el);
190	});
191	```
192	
193	## A way past the nav
194	
195	```html
196	<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
197	```
198	
199	```css
200	.skip { position: absolute; left: var(--space-md); top: calc(-1 * var(--space-3xl)); z-index: var(--z-toast); padding: var(--space-xs) var(--space-md); background: var(--color-ink); color: var(--color-paper); }
201	.skip:focus-visible { top: var(--space-md); }
202	```
203

